    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and real-world applications. As a student with a passion for history and art, I see math as a tool for understanding patterns in nature and society. It’s not my favorite subject, but I appreciate its logic and how it connects to other fields like philosophy and photography.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "I rarely get anxious about math because I approach it as a problem-solving challenge rather than a source of fear. My high conscientiousness and extraversion help me stay organized and confident. When I do feel a bit stressed, I use deep breathing to calm my nerves before tackling a problem.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used a free AI tool last month to check my algebra homework. It explained steps clearly and caught mistakes I missed. The experience was positive—helpful without overwhelming me. I’d recommend it for students who want quick clarification without the stress of traditional tutoring.",
